Falsifies `inter_process_communication::timer::verification::a_walk_fires_exactly_the_due_timers`.

The defect: expiry uses a strict comparison, so a timer whose deadline equals `now` does not fire
on this walk. It looks like an off-by-one that cannot matter, and the cache (`is_due` is `>=`)
disagrees with it, so a walk runs and fires nothing.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(fired[k], due)` for a timer armed at exactly `now`.

